  "regressions": [
    "Detailed Native descriptors validate access mode, openat base/path/symlink/exclusive flags and errors; open/dup choose lowest free descriptor.",
    "Dup shares file position and append status, while CLOEXEC is descriptor-local. Invalid flags and failed seek preserve state.",
    "tmpfs/ext2 append chooses EOF and publishes data/position under shared inode/data locking; unsupported backends reject append.",
    "A legacy detached ext2 seek regression was caught by full-suite execution and fixed before the final 1293-test pass.",
    "C strings, allocation ownership, unsigned bytes, ASCII ctype and C17 integer endptr/overflow/base behavior pass on both ext2/tmpfs fixtures.",
    "C variadic printf-family tests cross register save areas and stack arguments; buffer truncation, width/precision, integer limits, explicit unsupported formats and overflow tested.",
    "C streams test read/write, partial items, EOF/error, pushback, seek, fdopen ownership, append and error preservation.",
    "Unmodified zlib tests deterministic binary compress/uncompress, chunked deflate/inflate, gzip writes/printf/read/seek/positions/EOF, gzdopen descriptor ownership and CRC corruption diagnostics.",
    "Existing errno fault injection, C main startup, native std compilation/execution and two proc-macro DSOs/consumer continue passing."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "RV64 cross-build and ELF audit only; no new RV64 guest execution.",
    "Unbuffered stdio subset: no float/wide/positional/%n formatting, scanf or setvbuf; fixed C locale and C17 integer prefixes.",
    "Descriptor surface excludes pipe/dup2/unlink/chdir/getcwd additions; native signed seek currently tmpfs/ext2 only.",
    "Current permissions model does not implement POSIX ownership/classes/umask/enforcement; mode limited to0777.",
    "A syscall transfers at most64KiB; short I/O and 1024-byte UTF8 path limits remain.",
    "This is bounded real-library acceptance, not musl parity, complete POSIX/C SDK, signal safety or physical OOM recovery.",
    "Cargo and its dependencies remain outstanding. Published distribution bundle unchanged."
  ],
